 DR, playback, body-wrench and fixed-variant capability sources remain their existing instance APIs. The static inventory intentionally leaves those dependent entries unknown; `backend.get_capabilities()` aggregates authoritative instance declarations. Multiple logical entity partitions do not imply arbitrary multi-articulation composition. URDF investigations and unmerged branches are not current support. IsaacSim's legacy reserved zero contact buffer never means a valid contact query or absence of physical contact; mapped scenes serve declared geom-pair `contact data="force" reduce="netforce"` sensors through the dedicated PhysX pair-force slot and wildcard body-net force (`geom2` omitted) plus body-net `data="found"` flags through one batched per-entity PhysX contact view, while legacy model-file scenes fail all contact declarations closed. Isaac worker sensors support gyro reconstruction but reject accelerometers.
 
 The [capability design decision](adr-capabilities.md) defines evidence matching and snapshot lifetime. `available` in the installation table above is never a task compatibility decision.
+
+### TGS external force application (DexLab adapter extension)
+
+`isaacsim_external_forces_every_iteration=True` applies external forces at each native TGS position iteration via `PhysxSceneAPI`. The default `None` preserves SDK behavior; explicit `False` disables the option. The host and worker require an actual boolean and verify the USD readback. This changes force application timing, not the integration timestep or engine source. Validate affected dynamics before adoption; existing saved experiments retain their original configuration.
+
+### Mesh-backed SDF transport (DexLab adapter extension)
+
+The mapped IsaacSim path preserves MJCF `type="sdf"` intent separately from importer transport. A temporary sibling MJCF spells only mesh-backed SDF geoms as `mesh`; the native importer requires adjacent relative mesh resources and a USD-compatible filename. Role authoring then applies `PhysxSDFMeshCollisionAPI` with resolution 256 and sparse subgrid resolution 6. Native USD readback rejects missing SDF APIs or changed approximation/resolution. Both artifact identities include the transport version; role identities also include per-geom SDF intent. Optional absent geom slots remain collision-disabled placeholders. Plugin SDFs without a mesh are rejected. Ordinary mesh collision semantics are unchanged.
+
+This is a new SDF sampled from the source triangle surface, not a transfer of MuJoCo octree samples or equivalent contact mechanics. USD readback alone is not contact qualification: the DexLab torus/sphere protocol tests an open hole, support on the torus surface and an explicit convex-hull negative control. Official PhysX and IsaacLab sources are unchanged.
